  Split  jj split -r @ · chain 2 → 1 (2 becomes the parent of 1)                                    
                                                                                                    
    1   stays in @                                                                   │   2   new    
  4 hunks · +4 −2                                                                    │ empty        
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  
  file1.txt                                                                          │              
  ▌ @@ -1,3 +1,4 @@                                                                  │              
  ▌  line 1                                                                          │              
  ▌ +new line     ╭─ Welcome to jj-diff ─────────────────────────────────────────╮   │              
  ▌  line 2       │ One column per commit the split makes, the revision on the   │   │              
    @@ -10,2 +11,3│ left. Move changes into the columns, then apply.             │   │              
     line 10      │                                                              │   │              
    +another line │ space  select the hunk, or in visual the lines               │   │              
  file2.txt       │ >      move the selection one column right, or to a new one  │   │              
    @@ -0,0 +1,2 @│ 1–9    send the selection to column N                        │   │              
    +first line   │ d      describe the focused column                           │   │              
    +second line  │ enter  apply the split                                       │   │              
  file3.txt       │                                                              │   │              
